  *Scenario*: In the scratch script `run_mutants.sh`, the summary regex `grep -qE "[0-9]+ (failed|error)"` failed to match pytest's `-x` summary string `"stopping after 1 failures"`, causing `.scratch/dev-training/mutants.log` to print `"0 red / 22 total"`. Direct evaluation of test return codes confirmed that all 22 named mutants turn their tests strictly red (22/22 RED).
- **Finding F-02 (COSMETIC)** — [`tests/test_cf_dev.py:555`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-dev/tests/test_cf_dev.py#L555) (Verified by reading & execution)  
  *Scenario*: `assert float(loss2) > 0.0` converts a grad-tracking tensor to float without `.detach()`, emitting a harmless PyTorch `UserWarning`. Adding `.detach()` silences the warning.
- **Finding F-03 (COSMETIC)** — [`scripts/dev_e0_common.py:107-117`](file:///home/u24/papers/mcrl-leo-handover-dev/scripts/dev_e0_common.py#L107-L117) (Verified by reading)  
